may-007, an Oral TNFa Inhibitor for Inflammatory Bowel Disease\nMechanisms of Action: TNF Inhibitor\n...\nFDA Designation: *\nApproval Status: Not Approved\nApproved Countries: None\nApproved Indications: None\n...\nCompany: Hemay PTY\n...\nAdditional Commercial Interests: None", "date": "2024-03-02", "last_updated": "2025-06-17"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "OVERVIEW", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/app/sehk/2025/107914/a127807/sehk25120100842.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Hemay007.\nOur key product, Hemay007 is screened from a compound library directed by multiple pharmacological functional substructures and is a TNF-�small molecule regulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model, Hemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the diseased monkeys, and pathological examinations of the intestines after treatment revealed that the colon tissue almost returned to a normal state.\nAs of the Latest Practicable Date, we had completed the\nPhase II clinical trial for monotherapy for UC and were also conducting a Phase II clinical trial for RA.\nWe plan to prioritize the clinical trial for RA and currently do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps for UC.\n...\nWe discovered and developed Hemay022 and retained global rights for its development and commercialization.\n...\nHemay007 is screened from a compound library using multiple pharmacological approaches and is a TNF-�small molecule modulator.\nIn the spontaneous UC monkey model,\nHemay007 reduced the number of ulcers in the colons of the diseased monkeys.\n...\nFor the development of Hemay007, we will prioritize the clinical trial for RA.\nCurrently, we do not have a definitive timetable for the next steps in UC.\nWe do not currently have plans to initiate any additional clinical trials overseas in respect of Hemay007.\n...\nThe IND approval is\napplicable to all phases\nclinical trials of the use of\nHemay007 in 200mg\ntablets carried out in\nChina.(2)", "date": n