{"row_id": "q028", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression tumour shrinkage in Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma animal models", "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q028-2", "query": "HEC234055 PK-59 PDAC monotherapy tumour regression", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "HEC234055 PK-59 PDAC monotherapy tumour regression", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 25785.9, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] E262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4 - HKEXnews", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301899.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "Sub-nanomolar cell activity: In a variety of KRAS mutation-driven cancer cell lines, its anti-proliferative activity reaches the sub-nanomolar level, with half- maximal inhibitory concentration (‘‘IC50’’) as low as 0.49 nanomolar (‘‘nM’’), showing potent inhibitory capabilities superior to current benchmark molecules.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models\n(including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce\ndose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.\n...\nGood pharmacokinetics (PK) and excellent safety profile: Oral bioavailability is good across all preclinical species. The safety evaluation results show that hERG inhibition IC50>10 micromolar (‘‘μM’’), and the safety window in the 28-day GLP toxicology study is over 90 times.\n...\nThe preclinical research data disclosed in this announcement are derived from laboratory and animal model studies, and the relevant drug candidates have not yet undergone clinical trials\nin\nhumans.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-04-23"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Press Release", "url": "https://www.perspectivetherapeutics.com/newsroom/press-release?i=159323", "domain": "perspectivetherapeutics.com", "snippet": "For more information, activate the button labeled \"Explore your accessibility options\".\nNewsroom", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-28"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "CCDI Hub", "url": "https://moleculartargets.ccdi.cancer.gov/studies/phs003215", "domain": "moleculartargets.ccdi.cancer.gov", "snippet": "This system is provided for Government-authorized use only.\nUnauthorized or improper use of this system is prohibited and may result in disciplinary action and/or civil and criminal penalties.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-19"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma Archives - Annual Report - Ipsen", "url": "https://www.ipsen.com/annualreport/clinical_study_indications/pancreatic-ductal-adenocarcinoma/", "domain": "ipsen.com", "snippet": "Download the report\nA conversation with David Loew\nPress shift tab to select search category\n...\nNo", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-30"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "A potential therapeutic target for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022356525397867", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-03"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Lactate Dehydrogenase-A Inhibitor Against Pancreatic Cancer", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0223523424004781", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-02"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Page not found", "url": "https://medschool.cuanschutz.edu/colorado-cancer-center/clinical-trials/214C19E7-3028-64D9-A5BF-FF0A001CE385", "domain": "medschool.cuanschutz.edu", "snippet": "Monday–Thursday: 7:30 a.m.\n– 6:00 p.m.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-18"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic Cancer: Review of the Current and ...", "url": "https://www.jhoponline.com/issue-archive/2022-issues/december-2022-vol-12-no-6/pancreatic-cancer-review-of-the-current-and-investigational-drug-landscape", "domain": "jhoponline.com", "snippet": "Patients with unresectable PDAC have a significantly increased risk of relapse, as was shown in the PRODIGE 4/ACCORD 11 study of patients with metastatic PDAC.^9^ The 18-month PFS and OS were 3.3% and 18.6%, respectively, in the FOLFIRINOX cohort versus 0% and 6%, respectively, with gemcitabine alone, demonstrating a markedly reduced time to disease recurrence in patients who presented with unresectable PDAC versus patients presenting with resectable disease.^9^\nThe NCCN Guidelines do not list any preferred chemotherapy regimen for subsequent therapy in recurrent PDAC.^8^ Gemcitabine-based regimens for patients whose disease progressed after first-line treatment with FOLFIRINOX may be considered, but the available data consist mostly of small, retrospective analyses.^11-13^ Conversely, subsequent treatment with FOLFIRINOX after first-line gemcitabine-based therapy may be considered.^14-16^", "date": "2026-09-21", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma: Current and Evolving ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5535831/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Similarly, targeting of miR-21 using lentiviral vectors stimulated angiogenesis, enhanced gemcitabine delivery and provoked tumour regression [259,260,261].", "date": "2017-06-22", "last_updated": "2026-08-04"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Suppression of pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma growth and ...", "url": "https://www.broadinstitute.org/p