{"row_id": "q030", "objective": "SGR-4174 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma animal models", "anchors": ["SGR-4174"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q030-1", "query": "SGR-4174 Mia PaCa2 monotherapy tumour regression xenograft", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "SGR-4174 Mia PaCa2 monotherapy tumour regression xenograft", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 8890.9, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "SOS1: tracking the evolving path from promising to actionable ...", "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12943-026-02632-7?error=cookies_not_supported&code=89f85997-69de-41bd-b40a-f6985ed2b656", "domain": "link.springer.com", "snippet": "Mechanistically, SGR-4174 binds to the catalytic domain of SOS1, disrupting SOS1::KRAS^G12C^ PPI (IC~50~ of 13 nM) [80].\nPreclinical in vitro studies demonstrated that SGR-4174 administration (IC~50~ values ranging from 42 to107 nM) resulted in a robust impairment of RAS-mediated signal transduction and reduced cell viability (3D cell cultures) across a wide spectrum of human cancer cell lines harboring KRAS^G12C/D/V^ or EGFR mutations (since we had no access to the panel of the specific cells employed in this study, this information is not included in Supplementary Table 2) [80].\nIn KRAS^G12C^-mutated tumor xenograft models, including NSCLC and PDAC, single-agent administration of SGR-4174 elicited dose-dependent TGI (please note that we were unable to find the precise dosing regimens employed in this study) [80].\nIn addition, concomitant administration of SGR-4174 and Sotorasib resulted in a deeper and more sustained inhibition of KRAS signal transmission, pronounced inhibition of cell proliferation in 3D cell culture models, and tumor regression in xenograft models when compared to the respective monotherapies [80].\nFurthermore, along with Trametinib, SGR-4174 prevented the reactivation of the KRAS pathway, which is typically observed upon MEK inhibition, leading to increased tumor cell death and stasis [80].", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-19"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Schrödinger, Inc. - Drug pipelines, Patents, Clinical trials", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/ee6d0cc13d500f7740bc81b30e6d5978", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "In KRAS G12C tumor xenograft mouse models, SGR-4174 monotherapy demonstrated dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and a decrease in the tumor PD biomarker pERK.SGR-4174 was examined in combination with KRAS G12C inhibitor sotorasib and MEK inhibitor trametinib in vitro and in vivo.\nWhen combined with sotorasib, SGR-4174 demonstrated deeper and more sustained inhibition of the KRAS signaling pathway, stronger suppression of cell proliferation in 3D cell culture, and tumor regression in xenograft models compared to single agent activity.\n...\nSGR-4174 was well tolerated as monotherapy and in combination with sotorasib or trametinib.SGR-4174 demonstrated favorable PK properties across preclinical species and toxicity profile was well characterized.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] Schrödinger Presents New Preclinical Data at AACR Annual Meeting", "url": "https://s203.q4cdn.com/609444515/files/doc_news/Schrdinger-Presents-New-Preclinical-Data-at-AACR-Annual-Meeting-2025.pdf", "domain": "s203.q4cdn.com", "snippet": "The data also demonstrated that\nSGR-4174 has strong tumor growth inhibition as a monotherapy as well as in combination with MEK or KRAS inhibitors, while maintaining a favorable safety pro�le.\n...\nThe poster (Abstract #4376), “Preclinical characterization of SGR-4174, a potent and selective SOS1 inhibitor for the treatment of pan KRAS mutant cancers in combination with KRAS pathway inhibitors,” includes preclinical data demonstrating the superior binding, selectivity, and drug-like properties of SGR-4147 compared to MRTX0902 as assessed via comprehensive in vitro potency, ADME, and safety assays.\nThe preclinical data for SGR-4174 also show robust suppression of the RAS signaling pathway and potent cell killing activity across multiple cancer types harboring diverse KRAS mutations as well as EGFR and SOS1 mutations.\nSGR-4174 monotherapy achieved dose- dependent target engagement and tumor growth inhibition and induced tumor shrinkage when used in combination with MEK or KRAS inhibitors in preclinical models of pancreatic and non-small cell lung cancer.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-08"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Cloudflare", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/cancerres/article-pdf/60/14/3978/3239751/ch140003978p.pdf", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "snippet": "If you are using a CNAME origin record, make sure it is valid and resolvable.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2024-06-21"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Cloudflare", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/mct/article-pdf/17/8/1761/1858346/1761.pdf", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "snippet": "Cloudflare is currently unable to resolve your requested domain (aacrjournals.org).", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-11-03"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "MiA-PaCa2: Orthotopic pancreas tumor model - Reaction Biology", "url": "https://www.reactionbiology.com/sites/default/files/Downloads/service-related/in-vivo/xenograft/infosheets/MiA-PaCa2_ortho.pdf", "domain": "reactionbiology.com", "snippet": "Mice bearing orthotopically implanted MiA-PaCa2 tumors were treated with free or liposomal Gemcitabine.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-11-12"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "RESULT(S)", "url": "https://www.sedapds.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/2770-000_PS22-PosterTemplate_No2_v3.pdf", "domain": "sedapds.com", "snippet": "2. Predicted ORR from a single mouse was 99.9% (99%, \n100%) which was significantly higher than the ORR, \n37% (95%CI: 29-46) in the Phase II trial of non-small\ncell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients [6], Pred.\n(MIA-\nPaCa-2) in Figure 2\n• The inaccuracy was expected as the exposure-\n...\nimproved the correlation to clinical ORR – new \nprediction of ORR 50% (95%CI: 42-58), Pred.\n(MIA-", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-03-29"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "MIA PaCa-2 Xenograft Model", "url": "https://altogenlabs.com/xenograft-models/pancreatic-xenograft-models/miapaca-2-xenograft-model/", "domain": "altogenlabs.com", "snippet": "The MIA PaCa-2 cell line (human pancreas) is used to create the CDX (Cell Line Derived Xenograft) MIA PaCa-2 xenograft mouse model.\nThe MIA PaCa-2 xenograft model exhibits tumor growth inhibition and chemosensitization utilizing monotherapies or in combination (e.g. sulindac, LC-1, parthenolide, gemcitabine).", "date": "2023-03-07", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "���0�8s��dw�/獅�������k�i����xC��(��D�J�lj����}��*�*���PmWd�D�I�]SV79+�Ň���Uk�fcM�a�֪)Ǣtf֞Ԛl�b����ڑ��Sъ�c ,v�O� و�2���ar��NӬn�1註�ofB��P�žRcG�de�!>6�Q�>e��x�q듼��t&e6�Cy`����-|99��W�k5�M �i�rU�.��t�ʇ*��\"�����S����6�d>�d�-R��o��0ݻ��p���|ƶ�=κ��Ԫ��5&�̈O��w�����oL�w^�7��ӓ>]�'�Xq朱�3��H���B�A�BJ��h#.�âW�λ�y@{~�X�33�уgF�+�'ױ��;���r�%=��r�cxC9/��Z�<����~�bg�k�|K��f1SE��b���h�}fcZ\\�\\oL-B��X���j�K���7z���ܠK�%�K�u�8`g�Ч������R�ܸ�u��P<��dc�7�j�Y���g;o�I��%M�)�P��n��]�%���g�����6��=�ƞ �E�3;�nG�ga��%A��R� �2����(ϲ��T��t�(3�h��\\S>h �,��|�;+&��qi�����;U�e��`����\"�u����&s� +���Q+����7�,��~�w^�-�&$�f����6�:cY�8�X��/c]�☱��]K�� ��%M�n�7�7 ����:���z�9��b��Ş�-�v�#S&x��:��м��:�M�� K�R-,v�u�j�������&��o�%Z-�A'i>Pr�)���V��S�$�&X��y���Q�T9����f1��0�c(S��H(�mf�K\"Y/>�(-&�{�(;,c2>���0}�u���N�0xP����$Lk�U��^i��k'�uo���/b'��?q�\"y]5�?�V�q�h1x�3(��r�B����cՓ~�����d������2����ݙ>$S����W�Z\"I|�~�9bew-�P�(p➲��O�$�*��셓T�FSP>,�����]o,�}R��Ϛ���3�D��˦��0J���0���v��Wm�T����ť|g�