{"row_id": "q031", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q031-2", "query": "SPR2015 AsPC-1 xenograft tumour regression shrinkage", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "SPR2015 AsPC-1 xenograft tumour regression shrinkage", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 2572.5, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR2015: Merck Pays $400M, Up to $2.13B - novapharmanews.com", "url": "https://novapharmanews.com/apac/news/spr2015-merck-400m-2-13b-license", "domain": "novapharmanews.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is still preclinical.\nThe release cites nanomolar cell-line activity and tumor activity in xenograft models shown at AACR 2026, without a response rate.\n...\nIt also cites antitumor activity as a single agent in cell-derived and patient-derived xenografts, from preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR meeting.\nNo tumor-shrinkage percentage is printed.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Enters into Exclusive Global License Agreement ...", "url": "https://www.merck.com/news/merck-enters-into-exclusive-global-license-agreement-with-scibrunch-therapeutics-for-spr2015-an-investigational-oral-kras-g12d-on-inhibitor/", "domain": "merck.com", "snippet": "In addition, SPR2015 has demonstrated compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, as reported in preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-10-02", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "register", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/my-account/register?siteId=5148&returnUrl=https://academic.oup.com/carcin/article/41/10/1409/5697447", "domain": "academic.oup.com", "snippet": "This PDF is available to Subscribers OnlyView Article Abstract & Purchase Options\nFor full access to this pdf, sign in to an existing account, or purchase an annual subscription.", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-11-13"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "PDC000198 - Proteomic Data Commons - National Cancer Institute", "url": "https://proteomic.datacommons.cancer.gov/pdc/study/PDC000198", "domain": "proteomic.datacommons.cancer.gov", "snippet": "This warning banner provides privacy and security notices consistent with applicable federal laws, directives, and other federal guidance for accessing this Government system, which includes (1) this computer network, (2) all computers connected to this network, and (3) all devices and storage media attached to this network or to a computer on this network.\nThis system is provided for Government-authorized use only.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-22"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Breast Cancer Research and Treatment", "url": "https://deepblue.lib.umich.edu/handle/2027.42/44205", "domain": "deepblue.lib.umich.edu", "snippet": "More information about our policies and practices is available at Remediation of Harmful Language.", "date": "2001-09-07", "last_updated": "2025-04-07"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor's $2.13B Deal Tests Cross-Border Tech Transfer", "url": "https://www.pharmtech.com/view/kras-g12d-inhibitor-s-2-13b-deal-tests-cross-border-tech-transfer", "domain": "pharmtech.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 functions as an ON-state molecular glue, showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D cell lines with wild-type selectivity and tumor regression in xenograft models.\n...\nSPR2015 is described as a molecular glue inhibitor that engages the ON form of the mutant protein.^1^ It showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity across multiple KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining selectivity over wild-type cells, and it demonstrated monotherapy antitumor efficacy in cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Cloudflare", "url": "https://aacrjournals.org/clincancerres/article-pdf/23/3/623/2041560/623.pdf", "domain": "aacrjournals.org", "snippet": "Cloudflare is currently unable to resolve your requested domain (aacrjournals.org).", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-11-03"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Current Oncology Reports", "url": "https://www.springermedicine.com/current-oncology-reports/20483386", "domain": "springermedicine.com", "snippet": "*Current Oncology Reports* provides in-depth review articles contributed by international experts on the most significant developments in the field.", "date": "2025-01-26", "last_updated": "2025-03-27"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Cancer Cell", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1535610817300168", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-10-06"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Letter to the Editor:", "url": "https://journals.aboutscience.eu/index.php/cancerbreakingnews/article/view/206", "domain": "journals.aboutscience.eu", "snippet": "Please read the privacy information for details.\n...\nPlease read the privacy information for details.", "date": "2016-03-15", "last_updated": "2025-06-25"}], "raw": {"id": "54073e04-ccbb-49bf-a521-91d03bc9fd76"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:40:10+00:00"}
{"row_id": "q031", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q031-4", "query": "SPR2015 HPAC AsPC-1 xenograft AACR 2026 abstract 5978", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "SPR2015 HPAC AsPC-1 xenograft AACR 2026 abstract 5978", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 440.3, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Enters into Exclusive Global License Agreement ...", "url": "https://www.merck.com/news/merck-enters-into-exclusive-global-license-agreement-with-scibrunch-therapeutics-for-spr2015-an-investigational-oral-kras-g12d-on-inhibitor/", "domain": "merck.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is a potent and selective novel investigational preclinical molecular glue KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor that has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activities in various KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining good selectivity over KRAS wildtype cells.\n...\nIn addition, SPR2015 has demonstrated compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, as reported in preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-10-02", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Anirban Maitra on X: \"This #AACR26 abstract is worth $400 ...", "url": "https://x.com/Aiims1742/status/2104884186620494308", "domain": "x.com", "snippet": "Abstract 5978: SPR2015, a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor, exhibits favorable...\nAbstract.\nColorectal cancer (CRC) is the third most common malignancy and the second leading cause of cancer-related deaths worldwide.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck–SciBrunch SPR2015 Deal | Lucid Diligence Brief - LucidQuest", "url": "https://www.lqventures.com/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-deal-diligence-brief/amp/", "domain": "lqventures.com", "snippet": "SciBrunch’s AACR 2026 work reported tumor regression in PDAC/NSCLC mouse models and a 64.7% ORR and 94.1% DCR across a CRC CDX/PDX model panel, alongside favorable 28-day rodent tolerability.\n(AACR SPR2015 abstract)\n...\nSciBrunch says existing G12D inhibitors have yet to demonstrate clinically meaningful CRC monotherapy efficacy, while SPR2015 produced responses across its CRC xenograft panel.\n...\nSPR2015 was still preclinical and had not entered human testing.\nSciBrunch’s AACR 2026 abstract described it as IND-enabling and projected Phase 1 entry by the end of 2026.\n(AACR abstract 5978, Reuters)\n...\nSciBrunch reported nanomolar activity in KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines and tumor regression in mouse PDAC and NSCLC models.\nIn more than 15 CRC CDX/PDX models, the company reported a 64.7% ORR and 94.1% DCR, but these are preclinical animal-model results and should not be interpreted as patient response rates.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR2015: Merck Pays $400M, Up to $2.13B - novapharmanews.com", "url": "https://novapharmanews.com/apac/news/spr2015-merck-400m-2-13b-license", "domain": "novapharmanews.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is still preclinical.\nThe release cites nanomolar cell-line activity and tumor activity in xenograft models shown at AACR 2026, without a response rate.\n...\nIt also cites antitumor activity as a single agent in cell-derived and patient-derived xenografts, from preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR meeting.\nNo tumor-shrinkage percentage is printed.\n...\nXenograft activity does not establish a therapeutic index, and gastrointestinal or hematologic tolerability stays unknown until a first-in-human protocol reports laboratory and adverse-event tables.\n...\nThe release describes cell-line and xenograft results presented at AACR 2026 and does not give a human trial identifier or a first-dose date.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026 Annual Meeting Abstracts", "url": "https://cancer.uillinois.edu/news/aacr-2026-annual-meeting-abstracts", "domain": "cancer.uillinois.edu", "snippet": "The meeting, which was held April 17-22 in San Diego, California, gathered together scientists, clinicians, other health care professionals, survivors, patients and advocates to share the latest advances in cancer science and medicine.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck, SciBrunch Launch Up-to-$2.13B Collaboration ...", "url": "https://www.genengnews.com/topics/cancer/merck-scibrunch-launch-up-to-2-13b-collaboration-to-develop-preclinical-kras-inhibiting-molecular-glue/", "domain": "genengnews.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is a preclinical molecular glue, more specifically an oral KRAS G12D (ON) inhibitor that SciBrunch is developing for forms of cancer that include colorectal cancer (CRC), non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), and pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC)—the most common and aggressive type of pancreatic cancer.\n...\nAt the 2026 American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting, a team of SciBrunch researchers that included founder, chairman, and CEO Tao Hu, PhD, presented preclinical data showing SPR2015 to have demonstrated what it termed compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX and PDX) models.\n“SPR2015 is a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor with nanomolar proliferation inhibitory activities in various KRAS G12D cell lines while with good selectivity over KRAS wild type,” Hu and SciBrunch researcher colleagues reported in a poster presentation during AACR 2026.\nThey added that PR2015 was expected at the time to human Phase I studies by the end of this year.\nIn a head-to-head mouse study comparing a single oral once-daily dose at 100 mg/kg of SPR2015 to another unspecified G12D (ON) inhibitor in over 15 CRC CDX or PDX models, SPR2015 showed significantly superior efficacy in the *in vivo* CRC xenograft models, achieving a 64.7% objective response rate (ORR) and 94.1% disease control rate (DCR) as monotherapy.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Abstracts Annual Meeting 2026 | Meetings | AACR", "url": "https://www.aacr.org/meeting/aacr-annual-meeting-2026/abstracts-3/", "domain": "aacr.org", "snippet": "April 17 - 22, 2026San Diego Convention CenterSan Diego, California", "date": "2026-08-14", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Licenses SciBrunch's Preclinical Oral KRAS G12D ...", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/news/merck-licenses-scibrunch-s-preclinical-oral-kras-g12d-inhibitor-spr2015-in-2-13-billion-deal", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 (search)Search drug is a molecular glue inhibitor that showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D (search)Search target-mutant cell lines with selectivity over KRAS wild-type cells, plus monotherapy antitumor activity in xenograft models.\n...\nIn preclinical testing, SPR2015 (search)Search drug showed antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, according to preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.\nThe compound remains in preclinical development, and the September 28 announcement provided no human efficacy or safety results, did not identify the first cancer indication Merck (search)Search term will pursue, and set no first-in-human trial date.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-01"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026 | Oncology Congress Publications", "url": "https://www.oncpublications.com/AACR2026", "domain": "oncpublications.com", "snippet": "**April 17-22, 2026**\n## Agenda of oral and poster presentations at the 2026 American Association for Clinical Research (AACR) Annual Meeting", "date": "2026-01-28", "last_updated": "2026-07-03"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Enters $2.13 Billion License Agreement for ...", "url": "https://oncodaily.com/industry/merck-595856", "domain": "oncodaily.com", "snippet": "SPR2015 is a molecular glue–based inhibitor, still in preclinical development, designed to selectively target tumor cells carrying the KRAS G12D mutation.\n...\nIn preclinical testing, SPR2015 also demonstrated antitumor activity on its own in both cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models, with the data presented earlier this year at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.\n...\nSPR2015 is still an early-stage, preclinical asset, meaning substantial testing lies ahead before its safety and efficacy in humans are known.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}], "raw": {"id": "a856ac8f-c7f2-4b57-bf2b-b2ebc4edc431"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:40:10+00:00"}
