e Javascript in order to use PubChem website.\n...\nBefore sharing sensitive information, make sure you’re on a federal government site.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-05"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Molecular glue degraders - Articles - Page 5 | BioWorld", "url": "https://www.bioworld.com/articles/keyword/37115-molecular-glue-degraders?page=5", "domain": "bioworld.com", "snippet": "## IPS-06061: a molecular glue degrader of KRAS G12D with in vivo efficacy", "date": "2026-09-20", "last_updated": "2026-09-20"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Cancers du pancréas", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0928125818302997", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "try accessing the content again or\ncontact our support team\n...\nUse one of the supported browsers or contact our support team who will be happy to help.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-15"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "pancreatic tumor xenografts: Topics by Science.gov", "url": "https://www.science.gov/topicpages/p/pancreatic+tumor+xenografts", "domain": "science.gov", "snippet": "The overexpression of SSTR-1 significantly inhibited subcutaneous tumor size by 71% and 43% (n=5, p<0.05, t-test), and inhibited tumor weight by 69% and 47%, (n=5, p<0.05, t-test), in Panc-SSTR-1 and MIA-SSTR-1 groups, respectively, indicating the potent inhibitory effect of SSTR-1 on pancreatic cancer growth.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-19"}], "raw": {"id": "513e2aea-0398-4cae-a28a-62c4e12b699d"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:40:23+00:00"}
{"row_id": "q038", "objective": "KRAS G12D drugs approved against the target and their regulatory approval status", "anchors": ["ZE980277"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q038-2", "query": "ZE980277 KRAS G12D regulatory approval", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "ZE980277 KRAS G12D regulatory approval", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 1590.9, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Oral Investigational Agent Zoldonrasib Elicits Objective Responses ...", "url": "https://www.aacr.org/about-the-aacr/newsroom/news-releases/oral-investigational-agent-zoldonrasib-elicits-objective-responses-in-patients-with-kras-g12d-mutated-lung-cancer/", "domain": "aacr.org", "snippet": "CHICAGO – Patients with previously treated non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) whose tumors harbored a KRAS G12D mutation experienced clinical benefit from the oral KRAS G12D inhibitor zoldonrasib, according to results presented at the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting 2025, held April 25-30.\n...\nHowever, around 4% of NSCLC cases harbor KRAS G12D mutations, a mutation against which there are no approved targeted therapies, explained Kathryn C. Arbour, MD, an assistant attending and thoracic medical oncologist at Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, who presented the study.\n...\nZoldonrasib is a novel RAS(ON) tri-complex inhibitor that selectively targets the G12D mutation.\n...\nThe efficacy analysis included 18 patients with NSCLC who enrolled at least eight weeks before the data cutoff.\nAmong these patients, 61% had an objective response, and 89% experienced disease control.", "date": "2025-04-27", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor Molecule Overview", "url": "https://www.lillyoncologypipeline.com/molecule/kras-g12d-inhibitor/", "domain": "lillyoncologypipeline.com", "snippet": "The safety and efficacy of the agents for uses under investigation\nhave not been established.\nPipeline molecules may not receive\nregulatory approval and become commercially available for the uses\nbeing investigated.", "date": "2024-01-17", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS Inhibitor Clinical Trial Landscape, September 2026: 115 ...", "url": "https://datalookout.com/kras-inhibitor-clinical-trials", "domain": "datalookout.com", "snippet": "Revolution Medicines is leading the development of pan-RAS inhibitors that target multiple KRAS mutations simultaneously, including G12D, the dominant mutation in pancreatic cancer:\n...\n- **RMC-9805 (Revolution Medicines)**: KRAS G12D-selective.\nPhase 1 in KRAS G12D-mutant solid tumors, particularly PDAC.\n...\nThe broader KRAS-mutant population (G12D, G12V) remains without an approved targeted therapy.", "date": "2026-10-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-01"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D inhibitor (BeiGene) - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/3b644c9c621b47b9bf2d8979940c903f", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|Drug Highest PhasePreclinical|\n|First Approval Date-|\n...\nIn December 2022, the Company submitted the IND application for MRTX1133, a potent and selective KRASG12D inhibitor, which was cleared by the FDA in January 2023.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-04"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Investigational KRAS G12D Agents Demonstrate Promising ... - ILCN", "url": "https://www.ilcn.org/investigational-kras-g12d-agents-demonstrate-promising-antitumor-activity-in-non-small-cell-lung-cancer/", "domain": "ilcn.org", "snippet": "Zoldonrasib was previously granted breakthrough therapy designation by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in January 2026, marking the first time this designation was granted to an investigational drug specifically targeting the RAS G12D mutation.4 The FDA’s recent designation was based on data from the monotherapy cohort of the phase 1 RMC-9805-001 clinical trial, in which zoldonrasib demonstrated encouraging antitumor activity, along with acceptable safety and tolerability.4", "date": "2026-05-26", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor HRS-4642", "url": "https://www.cancerindex.io/drug/kras-g12d-inhibitor-hrs-4642", "domain": "cancerindex.io", "snippet": "Regulatory\n## Approvals (0)\nEach record names the authority, jurisdiction, indication text and status.\nA drug approved in one jurisdiction for one indication is not 'approved' in general.\nData not yet available\nNo regulatory approval recorded.\nAbsence here is not evidence of absence: only ingested jurisdictions are covered.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-19"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Our Pipeline - KRAS G12D inhibitor - Genentech", "url": "https://www.gene.com/medical-professionals/pipeline/kras-g12d-inhibitor", "domain": "gene.com", "snippet": "These compounds and their uses are investigational and have not been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.\nThis information is presented only for purposes of providing a general overview of clinical trials and should not be construed as a recommendation for use of any product for unapproved uses.", "date": "2019-12-19", "last_updated": "2026-09-28"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS Inhibitors Competitive Landscape Analysis 2026 | Eureka", "url": "https://eureka.patsnap.com/blog/life-science/kras-inhibitors-competitive-landscape-analysis-report-2026/", "domain": "eureka.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|Jacobio Pharmaceuticals|China|Tier 1 — Leader|Glecirasib (JAB-21822)|NMPA approval May 2025; partnered with AbbVie|", "date": "2026-05-18", "last_updated": "2026-09-22"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "US11964989B2 - KRas G12D inhibitors", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/US11964989B2/en", "domain": "patents.google.com", "snippet": "n 4).\n- KRas inhibitor has yet demonstrated sufficient safety and/or efficacy to obtain regulatory approval (e.g., see McCormick (2015) Clin Cancer Res. 21 (8):1797-1801).\n...\nctive amount of the compounds and methods of use therefor.\n- KRas G12D refers to a mutant form of a mammalian KRas protein that contains an amino acid substitution of an aspartic acid for a glycine at amino acid position 12.", "date": "2022-07-20", "last_updated": "2026-09-30"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Other KRAS G12D Targeted...", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/1759-7714.70203", "domain": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "snippet": "Although several G12D-targeted agents have entered clinical trials, none have yet been approved [64].", "date": "2025-12-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-01"}], "raw": {"id": "786f4b94-13f7-448d-a7be-78fb3f9124d3"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:40:24+00:00"}
{"row_id": "q038", "objective": "KRAS G12D drugs approved against the target and their regulatory approval status", "anchors": ["ZE980277"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q038-1", "query": "ZE980277 KRAS G12D approval status FDA EMA", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "ZE980277 KRAS G12D approval status FDA EMA", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 2864.7, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Search Orphan Drug Designations and Approvals - FDA", "url": "https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/opdlisting/oopd/detailedIndex.cfm?cfgridkey=1124625", "domain": "accessdata.fda.gov", "snippet": "|Generic Name:|KRAS G12D inhibitor|\n|--|--|\n|Date Designated:|05/01/2026|\n|Orphan Designation:|treatment of pancreatic cancer|\n|Orphan Designation Status:|Designated|\n|FDA Orphan Approval Status:|Not FDA Approved for Orphan Indication|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-11"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Oncology (Cancer)/Hematologic Malignancies Approval ...", "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/oncology-cancerhematologic-malignancies-approval-notifications", "domain": "fda.gov", "snippet": "|FDA approves sotorasib with panitumumab for KRAS G12C-mutated colorectal cancer|On January 16, 2025, the Food and Drug Administration approved sotorasib (Lumakras, Amgen Inc.) with panitumumab (Vectibix, Amgen Inc.) for adult patients with KRAS G12C-mutated metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC), as determined by an FDA-approved test, who have receive", "date": "2026-09-24", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Ongoing | Cancer Accelerated Approvals", "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/ongoing-cancer-accelerated-approvals", "domain": "fda.gov", "snippet": "|Krazati (adagrasib)|Adult patients with KRAS G12C-mutated locally advanced or metastatic non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), as determined by an FDA-approved test, who have received at least one prior systemic therapy.|12/12/2022|4378-1: Conduct a randomized comparative clinical trial of adagrasib in adult patients with KRAS G12", "date": "2026-09-17", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com · 2026 · 04KRAS Inhibitors (2026): The Complete Guide to Targeted Therapy...", "url": "https://cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com/2026/04/kras-inhibitors-2026-complete-guide-to.html", "domain": "cancer.aestheticsadvisor.com", "snippet": "Zoldonrasib is a covalent, G12D-selective RAS(ON) inhibitor and holds FDA Breakthrough Therapy Designation for KRAS G12D-mutated disease.\n...\nNo targeted therapy is currently FDA-approved specifically for RAS G12D-mutant cancers; zoldonrasib and related G12D-directed programs (including earlier-stage compounds such as MRTX1133) remain under active clinical investigation.\n...\nNot yet as a G12D-selective agent.\nDaraxonrasib's pancreatic cancer approval covers RAS G12-mutant disease broadly (including G12D and G12V) rather than being G12D-specific.\nZoldonrasib, a G12D-selective RAS(ON) inhibitor, remains investigational, with Phase 3 trials ongoing.\n...\n- No KRAS G12D-selective drug is yet approved anywhere; zoldonrasib is the most clinically advanced candidate, in Phase 3 development.", "date": "2026-09-07", "last_updated": "2026-09-29"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS Inhibitor Clinical Trial Landscape, September 2026: 115 ...", "url": "https://datalookout.com/kras-inhibitor-clinical-trials", "domain": "datalookout.com", "snippet": "Revolution Medicines is leading the development of pan-RAS inhibitors that target multiple KRAS mutations simultaneously, including G12D, the dominant mutation in pancreatic cancer:\n...\n- **RMC-9805 (Revolution Medicines)**: KRAS G12D-selective.\nPhase 1 in KRAS G12D-mutant solid tumors, particularly PDAC.", "date": "2026-10-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-01"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Medicines for human use under evaluation", "url": "https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/medicines/medicines-human-use-under-evaluation", "domain": "ema.europa.eu", "snippet": "Each month, the European Medicines Agency's (EMA) publishes an updated list of medicines for human use currently under evaluation by EMA’s Committee for Medicinal Products for Human Use (CHMP) to obtain a marketing authorisation in the European Union (EU).", "date": "2012-03-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Investigational KRAS G12D Agents Demonstrate Promising ... - ILCN", "url": "https://www.ilcn.org/investigational-kras-g12d-agents-demonstrate-promising-antitumor-activity-in-non-small-cell-lung-cancer/", "domain": "ilcn.org", "snippet": "Early findings from two clinical studies support the continued development of setidegrasib and zoldonrasib to target KRAS G12D mutations.\n...\nKRAS G12D mutations occur in around 5% of patients with NSCLC; however, there are currently no therapies available that specifically target these mutations.\n...\nZoldonrasib was previously granted breakthrough therapy designation by the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in January 2026, marking the first time this designation was granted to an investigational drug specifically targeting the RAS G12D mutation.4 The FDA’s recent designation was based on data from the monotherapy cohort of the phase 1 RMC-9805-001 clinical trial, in which zoldonrasib demonstrated encouraging antitumor activity, along with acceptable safety and tolerability.4", "date": "2026-05-26", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Zoldonrasib in Patients With KRAS G12D–Mutant NSCLC ...", "url": "https://ascopost.com/news/april-2026/zoldonrasib-in-patients-with-kras-g12d-nsclc-previously-treated-with-chemoimmunotherapy/", "domain": "ascopost.com", "snippet": "The investigational KRAS G12D inhibitor zoldonrasib had a favorable safety profile and induced antitumor activity in some patients with *KRAS * G12D–mutated non–small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) who were previously treated with chemotherapy and immunotherapy, according to preliminary findings from an ongoing phase I study presented at the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting 2026 (Abstract CT021).\n...\nTwo KRAS inhibitors have already been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) for the treatment of patients with *KRAS * G12C–mutated NSCLC.\nHowever, there are currently no RAS-targeted therapies available for patients with NSCLC harboring a *KRAS * G12D mutation.\nZoldonrasib is an oral G12D-selective tricomplex RAS(ON) inhibitor that is currently being studied in a phase I clinical trial of patients with solid tumors harboring *KRAS * G12D mutations who have received at least one prior line of therapy.\n...\nPrior results from this study showed encouraging safety and efficacy data in a NSCLC subgroup, which led to the agent receiving an FDA Breakthrough Therapy designation in January 2026.", "date": "2026-04-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Our Pipeline - KRAS G12D inhibitor - Genentech", "url": "https://www.gene.com/medical-professionals/pipeline/kras-g12d-inhibitor", "domain": "gene.com", "snippet": "These compounds and their uses are investigational and have not been approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration.", "date": "2019-12-19", "last_updated": "2026-09-28"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Therapeutic inhibition of RAS in non-small cell lung cancer - Frontiers", "url": "https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/oncology/articles/10.3389/fonc.2026.1817943/full", "domain": "frontiersin.org", "snippet": "As of this writing, both drugs retain their accelerated approvals, but neither have received full or standard FDA approvals based on these results, and neither study has easily interpretable OS results, limited by both sample size and crossover.\n...\n|Glecirasib (JAB-21822)|KRAS G12C|Inhibitor (covalent; GDP/Switch-II pocket)|NCT05009329 NCT05002270|JAB-21822-101 (phase 1) JAB-21822-1001 (phase 1/2)|\n...\n|Zoldonrasib (RMC-9805)|KRAS G12D (ON)|Molecular glue / tri-complex inhibitor (RAS(ON))|NCT06040541|RMC-9805-001 (phase 1/1b)|\n|ASP3082|KRAS G12D|PROTAC / targeted degrader|NCT05382559|ASP3082 first-in-human (phase 1)|", "date": "2026-06-30", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}], "raw": {"id": "2005a2f6-dafb-4a68-997c-46d1b425c448"}, "ts": "2026-10-03T12:40:26+00:00"}
