{"row_id": "q057", "objective": "CNP200137 first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "anchors": ["CNP200137"], "mode": "queries", "case_id": "q057-1", "query": "CNP200137 regulatory approval AML", "repeat": 0, "provider": "perplexity", "request": {"query": "CNP200137 regulatory approval AML", "search_type": "fast", "max_results": 10}, "ok": true, "status": 200, "error": null, "attempts": 1, "latency_ms": 1117.3, "n_results": 10, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Menin Inhibitor Drug Development Pipeline: AML, Diabetes ...", "url": "https://www.inflectionlabs.bio/reports/menin-inhibitor-pipeline", "domain": "inflectionlabs.bio", "snippet": "Revumenib and ziftomenib became the first approved menin inhibitors, treating KMT2A-rearranged and NPM1-mutant acute myeloid leukemias.\n...\n**3.\nCNP200137 (CoBX Bio, Pharos iBio)**\nThis is a pre-clinical stage, next-generation menin inhibitor that is designed to address menin resistance challenges.^[58]^ CNP200137 may well be the same molecule as CXB-001 with a different name, or a completely separate molecule being developed by the same South Korean biotech partnership.^[59]^", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Oncology (Cancer)/Hematologic Malignancies Approval ...", "url": "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/oncology-cancerhematologic-malignancies-approval-notifications", "domain": "fda.gov", "snippet": "venetoclax for newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia|On May 13, 2026, the Food and Drug Administration approved an oral combination of decitabine and cedazuridine tablets (Inqovi, Taiho Oncology, Inc.) with venetoclax for the treatment of newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukemia (AML) in adults 75 years or older, or who have comorbidities that preclude the use of intensive induction chemotherapy.|5/13/2026|", "date": "2026-09-24", "last_updated": "2026-10-02"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Acute Myeloid Leukemia: 2025 Update on Diagnosis, Risk-Stratification, and Management", "url": "https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/ajh.27625", "domain": "onlinelibrary.wiley.com", "snippet": "The FDA approved revumenib (SNDX−5613) for R/R *KMT2A* rearranged AML based on the results of AUGMENT-101, a phase I single agent clinical trial in *KMT2A*-rearranged and *NPM1*-mutated R/R AML [221].", "date": "2025-05-01", "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Circulars & Announcements-CStone Pharmaceuticals", "url": "https://www.cstonepharma.com/en/relation/notice14.html", "domain": "cstonepharma.com", "snippet": "Select “Accept all” for giving your consent to all cookies or select “Reject all” for using only strictly necessary cookies.", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-02-11"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "NCATS Inxight Drugs", "url": "https://drugs.ncats.io/substances?page=1333&facet=Development+Status/Clinical", "domain": "drugs.ncats.io", "snippet": "{{facet.count}}\n{{facet.count}}\n{{facet.count}}", "date": "2025-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-05-29"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Regulatory timeline - OnCo", "url": "https://onco.cc/regulatory/", "domain": "onco.cc", "snippet": "|20 Jul 2023|Quizartinib Small-molecule kinase inhibitor (FLT3-ITD, type II)|Approval|US|Frontline FLT3-ITD AML (QuANTUM-First)|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-03"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "CA A Cancer J Clinicians - 2024 - Kantarjian - Acute Myeloid ...", "url": "https://www.scribd.com/document/860905109/CA-A-Cancer-J-Clinicians-2024-Kantarjian-Acute-myeloid-leukemia-management-and-research-in-2025", "domain": "scribd.com", "snippet": "Since 2017, a turning point in AML research, 12 agentsYork, New York, USA have received regulatory approval for AML in the United States: venetoclax (BCL24 Karmanos Cancer Center, Wayne State inhibitor); gemtuzumab ozogamicin (CD33